  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/capital
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source explicitly frames disregards as special treatment of capital; this
      association does not identify every qualifying asset.
    evidence:
    - page: page/84/0035
      quote: "84351 [See DMG Memo 11/20] There are special rules for\n\n\n1. what capital is disregarded
        and\n\n\n2. the length of time that capital is disregarded 1.\n\n\n                          \
        \                     1 SPC Act 02, s 15(2) & s 15(6)(b); SPC Regs, reg 15(6) & Sch V"
      locator: DMG 84351
  - target: term/capital-disregard-evidence
    predicate: https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/ns#hasEvidenceRequirement
    rationale: The source describes a need to establish evidence for a disregard; operational
      evidence handling remains to be agreed.
    evidence:
    - page: page/84/0036
      quote: "84354 The person who has the capital has to show the capital can be disregarded. Capital
        is included\nwhen working out the amount of deemed weekly income if there is no evidence to show
        it can be\ndisregarded."
      locator: DMG 84354
  - target: term/capital-disregard-period
    predicate: https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/ns#hasDisregardPeriod
    rationale: The source separates duration categories from the existence of a disregard; no
      default duration is assigned.
    evidence:
    - page: page/84/0036
      quote: "84356 Capital which can be disregarded is disregarded for1\n\n\n1. an indefinite period
        (DMG 84367 et seq) or\n\n\n2. up to two years (DMG 84521 et seq) or\n\n\n3. a year or longer (DMG
        84561 et seq) or\n\n\n4. 26 weeks or longer (DMG 84601 et seq) or\n\n\n5. the remainder of an
        award of SPC (DMG 84671 et seq)."
      locator: DMG 84356
  - target: term/capital-valuation
    predicate: https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/ns#precedesAssessmentOf
    rationale: This models the sequence described by this captured paragraph, not a complete
      executable decision procedure.
    evidence:
    - page: page/84/0036
      quote: "84355 The DM decides if capital can be disregarded. This is done\n\n\n1. before the capital
        is valued as the DM does not have to know the value of the capital to decide if it can\nbe disregarded
        and\n\n\n2. before working out the amount of deemed weekly income from capital.\n\n\nThe DM also
        decides how long the capital is disregarded and, for certain disregards, whether it is\nreasonable
        to disregard the capital for a longer period."
      locator: DMG 84355
  - target: term/deemed-weekly-income
    predicate: https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/ns#precedesAssessmentOf
    rationale: This models the sequence described by this captured paragraph, not a complete
