    evidence:
    - page: page/84/0036
      quote: "84355 The DM decides if capital can be disregarded. This is done\n\n\n1. before the capital
        is valued as the DM does not have to know the value of the capital to decide if it can\nbe disregarded
        and\n\n\n2. before working out the amount of deemed weekly income from capital.\n\n\nThe DM also
        decides how long the capital is disregarded and, for certain disregards, whether it is\nreasonable
        to disregard the capital for a longer period."
      locator: DMG 84355
